// expect: trap
// A view is an iterator, so reading past its last element traps at the program's call, here after a
// `flatMap` whose last collection is empty and a `collect` defined at no element left.

main()
    val view = [1, 2, 3].view().flatMap(n -> if n < 3 then List(n) else List.empty[int]())
    print(view.toVector())
    val odd = [1, 2].view().collect(match
        n if n % 2 == 1 -> n)
    print(odd.next())
    print(odd.hasNext())
    view.next()
